halo-flash includes code adapted from the following MIT-licensed projects.
Each adapted file says so in its header; full license texts are in licenses/.

- gufo (Copyright (c) 2026 gufo contributors): src/core/gguf.{hpp,cpp},
  src/core/quant.{hpp,cpp}, the BPE merge loop in src/text/tokenizer.cpp,
  src/model/{config,weights,ngram,cpu_ops,reference}.{hpp,cpp},
  src/core/sampling.{hpp,cpp} (without its JSON grammar constraint), and parts of
  src/text/chat_template.cpp (from gufo src/models/qwen/chat_template.cpp: the
  Qwen3.8 prompt strings, Python-style trimming) and src/text/tool_call_parser.cpp
  (from gufo src/cli/serve/openai_chat.cpp: parameter framing, held tag prefixes,
  recovery after a malformed call, Python literal arguments).
- llama.cpp / ggml (Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors): quantized block
  layouts and dequantization in src/core/quant.cpp (via gufo).
- ds4 / DwarfStar (Copyright (c) 2026 the ds4.c authors): design references for
  n-gram disk reads, expert streaming and disk KV checkpoints (licenses/ds4.txt).

Test data (not code): tests/text/data/chat/flash_next.jinja is the
`tokenizer.chat_template` of the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GGUF (Qwen, with Unsloth's
template fixes), and qwen35.jinja the chat template of Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B-Base
(Apache-2.0). src/text/chat_template.cpp reproduces their output in C++.

Runtime dependency (not vendored): HRX System, Apache-2.0.
Test dependencies (fetched at build time): GoogleTest (BSD-3-Clause),
hegel-cpp (MIT) with its prebuilt libhegel engine.
